IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan (R.S.C., 1985, c. C-8) -- from the seat of the individual: the worker or self-employed person who
-- contributes, the contributor who claims a retirement or disability pension, and the survivor of a contributor.
-- "How much must I contribute? When can my pension start, and how much? Can I get a disability pension? What does my
-- family get when I die?" Facts are ones that person can state; the earnings record figures are on the person's
-- Statement of Contributions. The rules are in cpp-core.l4; this module builds the core's records from plain answers
-- and restates no rule.
--
-- Unofficial; not an official version. Contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence - Canada.
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Canada Pension Plan -- the contributor's and survivor's questions`

DECLARE `CPP amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `the amount, in Canadian dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no retirement pension` HAS `because` IS A `Retirement eligibility`
    `no disability pension` HAS `because` IS A `Disability eligibility`
    `no survivor's pension` HAS `because` IS A `Survivor eligibility`
    `no death benefit: the contributor did not meet the minimum qualifying period (s 44(3))`
    `not covered: a year before 2019, or a death before 2019`
    `not covered: the survivor also has a retirement pension (s 58(2))`

DECLARE `CPP contributions answer` IS ONE OF
    `my contributions are` HAS `contributions` IS A `Contributions`
    `not covered: a year before 2019`

GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `YMPE` IS A NUMBER, `months` IS A NUMBER, `wages` IS A NUMBER, `self-employed` IS A NUMBER, `resident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Contribution year`
`the contribution year from my answers` `year` `YMPE` `months` `wages` `self-employed` `resident` MEANS
    `Contribution year` WITH
        `year`                                       IS `year`
        `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings`        IS `YMPE`
        `months of the year that count`              IS `months`
        `contributory salary and wages`              IS `wages`
        `contributory self-employed earnings`        IS `self-employed`
        `resident in Canada for the Income Tax Act`  IS `resident`

GIVEN `average` IS A NUMBER, `first` IS A NUMBER, `second` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pensionable earnings record`
`the earnings record from my answers` `average` `first` `second` MEANS
    `Pensionable earnings record` WITH
        `average monthly pensionable earnings`           IS `average`
        `first additional monthly pensionable earnings`  IS `first`
        `second additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS `second`

§§ `Part I -- my contributions`

@export How much must I contribute to the Canada Pension Plan for a year, as an employee and on self-employed earnings (ss 8, 10, 16-20; Schedules 1 and 2)?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year, 2019 or later (for example 2026)
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings (YMPE) for that year, in Canadian dollars, as published for the year
      `months of the year that count` IS A NUMBER @desc 12, unless in that year you turned 18 or 70 (count the months after you turned 18, or before you turned 70) or your contributory period ended or began again because of disability
      `my employment income from pensionable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your salary and wages for the year from pensionable employment in Canada (outside Quebec), before deductions; one employer is assumed
      `my self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net self-employment earnings for the year (0 if none)
      `I was resident in Canada for income tax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in Canada for income tax purposes in the year (self-employed contributions apply only then)
GIVETH A `CPP contributions answer`
`What must I contribute to the CPP` `the year` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `months of the year that count` `my employment income from pensionable employment` `my self-employed earnings` `I was resident in Canada for income tax` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the contributions for the year` (`the contribution year from my answers` `the year` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `months of the year that count` `my employment income from pensionable employment` `my self-employed earnings` `I was resident in Canada for income tax`)
    WHEN JUST `c` THEN `my contributions are` `c`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: a year before 2019`

@export What is the total I must contribute to the Canada Pension Plan for a year (all six contributions together)?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year, 2019 or later
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings (YMPE) for that year, in Canadian dollars
      `months of the year that count` IS A NUMBER @desc 12, unless in that year you turned 18 or 70, or your contributory period ended or began again because of disability
      `my employment income from pensionable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your salary and wages for the year from pensionable employment, before deductions
      `my self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net self-employment earnings for the year (0 if none)
      `I was resident in Canada for income tax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in Canada for income tax purposes in the year
GIVETH A `CPP amount answer`
`What is my total CPP contribution` `the year` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `months of the year that count` `my employment income from pensionable employment` `my self-employed earnings` `I was resident in Canada for income tax` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the contributions for the year` (`the contribution year from my answers` `the year` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `months of the year that count` `my employment income from pensionable employment` `my self-employed earnings` `I was resident in Canada for income tax`)
    WHEN JUST `c` THEN `the amount, in Canadian dollars, is` (`to the cent` (`the total contributions` `c`))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: a year before 2019, or a death before 2019`

§§ `Part II -- my retirement pension`

@export Can I be paid a Canada Pension Plan retirement pension (ss 2, 44(1)(a), 60)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `I have made a CPP contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever made a CPP contribution as an employee or on self-employed earnings (or had pensionable earnings credited to you on a separation or divorce)
GIVETH A `Retirement eligibility`
`Can I get a CPP retirement pension` `my age` `I have made a CPP contribution` MEANS
    `the retirement pension eligibility` `my age` `I have made a CPP contribution`

@export If I apply now, from what age (in months) can my CPP retirement pension be paid (s 67(3.1))?
GIVEN `my age when I apply, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in the month you apply, in months, counting the month of a birthday as the start of that year of age (for example 63 years and 4 months is 760)
      `the age I choose for it to start, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc The age (in months, as above) you ask for the pension to start in your application, or 0 if you do not choose
GIVETH A NUMBER
`From what age can my CPP pension start` `my age when I apply, in months` `the age I choose for it to start, in months` MEANS
    `the first month of the retirement pension` `my age when I apply, in months` `the age I choose for it to start, in months`

@export How much will my monthly CPP retirement pension be, with the reduction for starting before 65 or the increase for starting after (s 46; Regulations ss 78.3, 78.4)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when the pension starts
      `I have made a CPP contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever made a CPP contribution
      `my average monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your average monthly pensionable earnings for the base CPP, as the Record of Earnings gives them (after the general drop-out and child-rearing drop-out), in Canadian dollars
      `my first additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your first additional monthly pensionable earnings (the enhancement from 2019), in Canadian dollars (0 if none)
      `my second additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your second additional monthly pensionable earnings (the enhancement from 2024), in Canadian dollars (0 if none)
      `my age when it starts, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in the month the pension starts, in months (65 years exactly is 780; 60 years is 720; 70 years is 840)
GIVETH A `CPP amount answer`
`How much is my CPP retirement pension` `my age` `I have made a CPP contribution` `my average monthly pensionable earnings` `my first additional monthly pensionable earnings` `my second additional monthly pensionable earnings` `my age when it starts, in months` MEANS
    LET `eligibility` MEANS `the retirement pension eligibility` `my age` `I have made a CPP contribution`
    IN CONSIDER `eligibility`
       WHEN `a retirement pension is payable on application (s 44(1)(a))` THEN
            `the amount, in Canadian dollars, is` (`the monthly retirement pension` (`the earnings record from my answers` `my average monthly pensionable earnings` `my first additional monthly pensionable earnings` `my second additional monthly pensionable earnings`) `my age when it starts, in months`)
       OTHERWISE `no retirement pension` `eligibility`

§§ `Part II -- a disability pension (situation: you have a disability that stops you working)`

GIVEN `last six` IS A NUMBER, `in all` IS A NUMBER, `since previous` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Disability contribution record`
`the disability record from my answers` `last six` `in all` `since previous` MEANS
    `Disability contribution record` WITH
        `qualifying years among the last six`             IS `last six`
        `qualifying years in all`                         IS `in all`
        `contributed every year since a previous disability benefit ceased` IS `since previous`

@export Can I be paid a Canada Pension Plan disability pension (ss 42(2), 44(1)(b), 44(2))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `a CPP retirement pension is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are already receiving a CPP (or QPP) retirement pension
      `my disability is determined to be severe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your disability is (or would be) determined to make you incapable regularly of pursuing any substantially gainful occupation
      `my disability is determined to be prolonged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your disability is (or would be) determined to be likely to be long continued and of indefinite duration, or likely to result in death
      `years of the last six with contributions on earnings above the exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the last six calendar years of your contributory period, how many years you contributed on earnings of at least 10% of that year's YMPE (shown on your Statement of Contributions)
      `years in all with contributions on earnings above the exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc How many calendar years in all you contributed on earnings of at least 10% of that year's YMPE
      `I contributed every year since an earlier disability benefit stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an earlier CPP disability benefit and have contributed in every year since it stopped (no if you never had one)
GIVETH A `Disability eligibility`
`Can I get a CPP disability pension` `my age` `a CPP retirement pension is payable to me` `my disability is determined to be severe` `my disability is determined to be prolonged` `years of the last six with contributions on earnings above the exemption` `years in all with contributions on earnings above the exemption` `I contributed every year since an earlier disability benefit stopped` MEANS
    `the disability pension eligibility` `my age` `a CPP retirement pension is payable to me` `my disability is determined to be severe` `my disability is determined to be prolonged`
        (`the disability record from my answers` `years of the last six with contributions on earnings above the exemption` `years in all with contributions on earnings above the exemption` `I contributed every year since an earlier disability benefit stopped`)

@export How much is my monthly CPP disability pension (s 56)?
GIVEN `the flat rate benefit this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The flat rate portion of the CPP disability pension for the year, as published (it is indexed each year), in Canadian dollars
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `a CPP retirement pension is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are already receiving a CPP (or QPP) retirement pension
      `my disability is determined to be severe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your disability is (or would be) determined to be severe (incapable regularly of any substantially gainful occupation)
      `my disability is determined to be prolonged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your disability is (or would be) determined to be prolonged (long continued and of indefinite duration, or likely to result in death)
      `years of the last six with contributions on earnings above the exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the last six calendar years of your contributory period, how many you contributed on earnings of at least 10% of the YMPE
      `years in all with contributions on earnings above the exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc How many calendar years in all you contributed on earnings of at least 10% of the YMPE
      `I contributed every year since an earlier disability benefit stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have contributed in every year since an earlier CPP disability benefit stopped (no if you never had one)
      `my average monthly pensionable earnings to the month of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc Your average monthly pensionable earnings over your contributory period up to the month you became disabled (at least 48 months counted), in Canadian dollars
      `my first additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your first additional monthly pensionable earnings (0 if none)
      `my second additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your second additional monthly pensionable earnings (0 if none)
GIVETH A `CPP amount answer`
`How much is my CPP disability pension` `the flat rate benefit this year` `my age` `a CPP retirement pension is payable to me` `my disability is determined to be severe` `my disability is determined to be prolonged` `years of the last six with contributions on earnings above the exemption` `years in all with contributions on earnings above the exemption` `I contributed every year since an earlier disability benefit stopped` `my average monthly pensionable earnings to the month of disability` `my first additional monthly pensionable earnings` `my second additional monthly pensionable earnings` MEANS
    LET `eligibility` MEANS `Can I get a CPP disability pension` `my age` `a CPP retirement pension is payable to me` `my disability is determined to be severe` `my disability is determined to be prolonged` `years of the last six with contributions on earnings above the exemption` `years in all with contributions on earnings above the exemption` `I contributed every year since an earlier disability benefit stopped`
    IN CONSIDER `eligibility`
       WHEN `a disability pension is payable on application (s 44(1)(b))` THEN
            `the amount, in Canadian dollars, is` (`the monthly disability pension` `the flat rate benefit this year` (`the earnings record from my answers` `my average monthly pensionable earnings to the month of disability` `my first additional monthly pensionable earnings` `my second additional monthly pensionable earnings`))
       OTHERWISE `no disability pension` `eligibility`

@export How many months before the month I apply can my CPP disability pension begin (ss 42(2)(b), 69)? A negative answer means after.
GIVEN `months from the month I became disabled to the month I apply` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months before the month of your application you became disabled (0 if in the same month)
      `I received a CPP disability pension in the five years before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received a CPP or QPP disability pension at any time in the five years before you became disabled this time
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How far back can my CPP disability pension be paid` `months from the month I became disabled to the month I apply` `I received a CPP disability pension in the five years before` MEANS
    `months before the application that the disability pension can start` `months from the month I became disabled to the month I apply` `I received a CPP disability pension in the five years before`

§§ `Part II -- after a contributor's death (situation: your spouse or common-law partner, a CPP contributor, has died)`

@export Am I entitled to a CPP survivor's pension (ss 42(1), 44(1)(d), 44(3), 44.1, 44.2)?
GIVEN `my relationship to the contributor at death` IS A `Relationship at death` @desc One of: the common-law partner at death; married at death, and there was no common-law partner; married at death, but the contributor had a common-law partner; neither
      `years the contributor made base contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar years in which the contributor made CPP base contributions
      `years in the contributor's contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar years in the contributor's contributory period (from age 18, or 1966, to death or the start of a retirement pension, leaving out years excluded for disability)
      `I was convicted of the contributor's murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of the first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor
      `our pensionable earnings were divided after 2024 and we did not live together again for a year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on or after 1 January 2025, your and the contributor's CPP earnings were split on a separation or divorce, and you had not lived together again in a conjugal relationship for a continuous year before the death
GIVETH A `Survivor eligibility`
`Can I get a CPP survivor's pension` `my relationship to the contributor at death` `years the contributor made base contributions` `years in the contributor's contributory period` `I was convicted of the contributor's murder or manslaughter` `our pensionable earnings were divided after 2024 and we did not live together again for a year` MEANS
    `the survivor's pension eligibility` `my relationship to the contributor at death`
        (`meets the s 44(3) minimum qualifying period` `years the contributor made base contributions` `years in the contributor's contributory period`)
        `I was convicted of the contributor's murder or manslaughter` `our pensionable earnings were divided after 2024 and we did not live together again for a year`

@export How much is my monthly CPP survivor's pension, if I have no CPP retirement pension of my own (s 58(1)(a.1), (b))?
GIVEN `the flat rate benefit this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The flat rate portion of the survivor's pension for the year (survivors under 65), as published, in Canadian dollars
      `my relationship to the contributor at death` IS A `Relationship at death` @desc One of: the common-law partner at death; married at death, and there was no common-law partner; married at death, but the contributor had a common-law partner; neither
      `years the contributor made base contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar years in which the contributor made CPP base contributions
      `years in the contributor's contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar years in the contributor's contributory period
      `I was convicted of the contributor's murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of the murder or manslaughter of the contributor
      `our pensionable earnings were divided after 2024 and we did not live together again for a year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your CPP earnings were split after 2024 without a year of living together again before the death
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years this month
      `I have a CPP retirement pension of my own` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a CPP or QPP retirement pension is payable to you (if yes, a different rule applies that is not covered)
      `the contributor's retirement pension` IS A NUMBER @desc The contributor's retirement pension as the Act computes it for the survivor's pension (the pension being paid at death, or 25% of their average monthly pensionable earnings plus the additional portions, indexed to this year), in Canadian dollars a month
GIVETH A `CPP amount answer`
`How much is my CPP survivor's pension` `the flat rate benefit this year` `my relationship to the contributor at death` `years the contributor made base contributions` `years in the contributor's contributory period` `I was convicted of the contributor's murder or manslaughter` `our pensionable earnings were divided after 2024 and we did not live together again for a year` `my age` `I have a CPP retirement pension of my own` `the contributor's retirement pension` MEANS
    LET `eligibility` MEANS `Can I get a CPP survivor's pension` `my relationship to the contributor at death` `years the contributor made base contributions` `years in the contributor's contributory period` `I was convicted of the contributor's murder or manslaughter` `our pensionable earnings were divided after 2024 and we did not live together again for a year`
    IN CONSIDER `eligibility`
       WHEN `a survivor's pension is payable on application (s 44(1)(d)(ii))` THEN
            CONSIDER `the monthly survivor's pension` `my age` `I have a CPP retirement pension of my own` `the flat rate benefit this year` `the contributor's retirement pension`
            WHEN JUST `x` THEN `the amount, in Canadian dollars, is` `x`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: the survivor also has a retirement pension (s 58(2))`
       OTHERWISE `no survivor's pension` `eligibility`

@export How much is the CPP death benefit paid to the contributor's estate (ss 44(1)(c), 44(3), 57)?
GIVEN `the year of death` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the contributor died
      `years the contributor made base contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar years in which the contributor made CPP base contributions
      `years in the contributor's contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar years in the contributor's contributory period
      `the contributor had received a CPP retirement or disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contributor ever received a CPP or QPP retirement pension or disability pension
      `a survivor's pension is payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a CPP survivor's pension is payable because of this death
GIVETH A `CPP amount answer`
`How much is the CPP death benefit` `the year of death` `years the contributor made base contributions` `years in the contributor's contributory period` `the contributor had received a CPP retirement or disability pension` `a survivor's pension is payable` MEANS
    LET `qualified` MEANS `meets the s 44(3) minimum qualifying period` `years the contributor made base contributions` `years in the contributor's contributory period`
    IN IF NOT (`qualified`)
       THEN `no death benefit: the contributor did not meet the minimum qualifying period (s 44(3))`
       ELSE CONSIDER `the death benefit` `the year of death` `qualified` `the contributor had received a CPP retirement or disability pension` `a survivor's pension is payable`
            WHEN JUST `x` THEN `the amount, in Canadian dollars, is` `x`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: a year before 2019, or a death before 2019`
